he pages sent stay; GitLab's `queryComplexity` of the first page logged at info), `job_page.rs` (`JobPage::built`: `https://<host[:port]>` + a path matching `/<segments>/-/jobs/<digits>`, segments of `[A-Za-z0-9._~-]`, none empty or `..`). Depends on `yamt-gitio` among `yamt-*` (may use `yamt-range` and `yamt-merge-core`), never tauri (`scripts/arch-check.sh`); no Mutex, nothing cached. Tests: unit tests in `detect.rs`, `job_page.rs`, `project.rs`, `query.rs`, `list.rs` (paging with an injected fetcher), `page/tests.rs` (over `tests/glab/merge-requests/`'s recorded pages); `tests/list.rs` (the fake glab, scenarios `merge-requests/`, `merge-requests-timeout/`, `logged-out/`), `tests/detect.rs` (real repositories; `GITLAB_HOST`/`GL_HOST` in a child process).
